-- title:
--   An O/𝔪-rational crossing point is closed with residue field O/𝔪
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a term $\mathfrak X$ of the structure `DRModelPackage p`, which bundles properness, flatness, integrality and normality of `DRModel.toBase p` (the structure morphism of the two-chart integral model over $\mathbb Z$ of the full modular function field at $p$ with its Igusa $j$), curve models of this function field over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with Galois and specialisation compatibilities, two sections `εinf`, `εzero`, a smooth locus, and the further data including the morphisms `𝔛.compInf` and `𝔛.compZero`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and $toκ : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism, and let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of `𝔛.compInf κ` and `𝔛.compZero κ`, with image `𝔛.crossingPt O κ toκ n` in $\mathfrak X_O :=$ `baseChangeO p O`, the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$, obtained by applying the underlying map of the first projection followed by `𝔛.compInf κ` followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`. Assume the two specialisation relations $\mathfrak X.ξinf \leadsto \mathfrak X.crossingPt$ and $\mathfrak X.ξzero \leadsto \mathfrak X.crossingPt$, and assume that this crossing point is $O/\mathfrak m$-rational: there is a morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak m) \to \mathfrak X_O$ whose composite with the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $O \to O/\mathfrak m$ and which sends the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak m)$ to `𝔛.crossingPt O κ toκ n`. Then the map sending $o \in O$ to the residue class, in the residue field of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at this crossing point, of the germ there of the global function on $\mathfrak X_O$ obtained by pulling $o$ back along $\mathfrak X_O \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ is surjective, and the singleton $\{$`𝔛.crossingPt O κ toκ n`$\}$ is closed in the underlying space of $\mathfrak X_O$. The proof visibly discards the hypotheses $5 \le p$, the description of the maximal ideal of $O$, and the two specialisation hypotheses, using only the rationality hypothesis.
--
--   This is the standard fact that an $O/\mathfrak m$-rational point of a scheme over a local ring $O$ is a closed point whose residue field is generated by the image of $O$, specialised to the crossing points of the geometric special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model after base change to $O$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart), where local coordinates at a crossing are produced and the residue field of the crossing must be identified with $O/\mathfrak m$.
